When generating Git commit messages for this repository, follow this format exactly.

## Structure

1. Heading — one short line (max 50 chars). Imperative mood. States what changed, not how.
2. Blank line.
3. Bullets (optional) — only when heading alone is insufficient. Max 3 bullets, one line each.

## Rules

- Heading must stand alone; reader gets intent without bullets.
- Bullets add why or scope, not repeat the heading.
- No paragraphs, no filler ("also", "just", "updated various").
- No file lists unless the commit is purely mechanical (rename/move).

## Format

<short imperative heading>

- <reason or context>
- <notable trade-off or scope limit>

## Good examples

Add theme token module for shared colors and spacing

- Centralizes hardcoded values from main.rs and theme.rs
- No runtime behavior change

Fix scanner crash on empty plugin paths

- Guard against zero-length path before native call

Refactor sidebar layout into dedicated component

## Bad examples (do not use)

Fixed some stuff and cleaned up code

Add theme tokens

Added a new theme token module that extracts color and size constants from multiple files across the codebase to improve maintainability and reduce duplication going forward.

Update main.rs, theme.rs, scanner/mod.rs, add tokens
